5,1,1,talk,Mizuki,,I believe we should start by understanding how our previous projects actually served the users. I'll look into the post-occupancy review ratings and the survey findings in the older blocks.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Victoria,,"I agree with Mizuki. To see the full picture, I want to examine the booking data for specialist and general rooms and the timetable records on rooms out of service.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Benjamin,,A prudent start. I shall examine the decade of delivery schedules by project rationale and the weather days in the site diaries to see why our timelines often drift.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Kenji,,I want to know if the money we plan for is actually what we spend! I'll check the tender records over three budget cycles and the renewal reserve for equipment.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Shunichi,,I'm interested in the people doing the work. I will look into the staffing posts since the hiring freeze and the bench technicians' weekly manual routines.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
