30,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"It seems we have a blind spot. Projects that benefit a single wing are rated poorly, while shared spaces are loved. Also, ground-floor work in old blocks often hits hazardous materials.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"My findings are concerning. General rooms are overcapacity while specialist ones sit idle. Worse, any room we take out of service requires expensive off-site hired space.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"As I suspected, ""appeal"" projects are a fantasy; they slip by a year. Additionally, outdoor work is heavily impacted by rain and frost, costing us weeks of progress.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"This is exactly what I feared! Mechanical costs are rising sharply, and we have no reserve for replacing old AV equipment. The budget on paper isn't the reality.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"We have a mismatch. Front-of-house and grounds staff are missing, but our bench technicians are wasting hours on manual routines because the equipment is outdated.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Victoria, if general rooms are overcapacity and shared spaces are rated highest, we should prioritize a project that increases general-purpose accessibility.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Mizuki, I agree, but we must avoid taking rooms out of service if we can't afford the off-site rentals. We need a plan with minimal timetable disruption.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, the rising mechanical costs you mentioned make the ""appeal"" projects even more dangerous. We need something that is a necessity, not a luxury, to stay on schedule.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, exactly! And if we pick something with high-tech gear, we need to know where the replacement money comes from, or it's just a future debt.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Mizuki, @Victoria, while you discuss space, remember the staff. If we don't pick a project that relieves the technicians' manual burden, we are just adding to their stress.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Mizuki"",""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Shunichi, I don't ignore the staff, but a project that fails or slips by a year creates more chaos for everyone. We need a deliverable win.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Shunichi, I understand the burden, but we cannot ignore the cost of hired space. Any plan must be surgically precise in its execution.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems we are all describing a systemic fragility. We need a candidate that is a necessity, avoids the weather, and doesn't trigger a year-long slip.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Kenji,,And it has to be financially realistic! No more pretending that mechanical plant costs are static.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"If the project automates those manual routines I found, it solves a real problem for the people actually running this campus.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
