55,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"Looking at the options, the Central Study Commons (A) fits the need for shared space, but it's in a ground-floor hall, which risks those hazardous materials I found.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"The Media Production Center (B) uses specialist rooms, which my data shows are already underused. The Path Network (C) is outdoor work, which is a timetable nightmare.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, @Mizuki, the Path Network (C) is also exposed to the weather, which I know causes massive delays. The Laboratory Ventilation Upgrade (D) is a necessity, not ""appeal.""","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Victoria"",""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"Plan D involves mechanical and ducted plant, which I found are rising in cost. However, it's better than Plan B, which would need AV reserves we don't have.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,Plan D is the only one that helps my technicians. Upgrading the extraction equipment eliminates those manual routines they are currently forced to do.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Shunichi, if Plan D is a necessary infrastructure upgrade, it's less likely to slip by a year than a ""comfort"" project like the Commons or the Paths.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Mizuki, I'm worried about the labs being out of service for Plan D. But if it's a necessity, we can plan the hired space more effectively than a luxury.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Plan D is the most rational. It avoids the weather risks of C and the ""appeal"" trap of A. It is a functional requirement, which usually means a more stable schedule.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Kenji,,I can accept the higher mechanical costs of Plan D because it's an essential upgrade. It's more honest than pretending a new lounge is a priority.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,It's the only choice that respects the staff. We cannot keep asking technicians to do manual window-opening because the vents are broken.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,"I agree. Between the risk of hazardous materials in Plan A and the weather in Plan C, Plan D is the most predictable path to a successful result.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Victoria,,"If we all agree that the operational relief and the necessity of the upgrade outweigh the temporary room loss, I am convinced.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,The logic is seamless. Plan D avoids the pitfalls of biological or aesthetic ambition and focuses on the core infrastructure.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Kenji,,I'm on board! Let's pick the one that actually fixes something broken rather than just adding something pretty.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,I am satisfied. Plan D provides the only tangible relief for the shrinking staff.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,4,talk,Mizuki,,I vote for Plan D.,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,4,talk,Victoria,,I vote for Plan D.,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,I vote for Plan D.,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,4,talk,Kenji,,I vote for Plan D!,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,I vote for Plan D.,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
